WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.690 --> 00:00:04.700
Is "No Way Home" the most emotionally devastating
"Spider-Man" film to date?

00:00:04.700 --> 00:00:05.840
No doubt about it.

00:00:05.840 --> 00:00:09.369
Keep watching for a rundown of the film's
most emotional moments.

00:00:09.369 --> 00:00:11.540
Major spoilers ahead!

00:00:11.540 --> 00:00:15.329
Many fan theories about "Spider-Man: No Way
Home" proved to be accurate, especially that

00:00:15.329 --> 00:00:18.020
Tobey Maguire and Andrew Garfield would appear.

00:00:18.020 --> 00:00:22.470
From the time they arrive, Maguire and Garfield
serve as mentors to Tom Holland's Peter Parker,

00:00:22.470 --> 00:00:25.220
teaching him that they've also experienced
immense losses.

00:00:25.220 --> 00:00:29.000
Fortunately, they'll be by his side when it
comes to fighting off the remaining villains

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:31.590
and curing them of their various ailments.

00:00:31.590 --> 00:00:35.659
As expected, they save the day, but sadly
it's at a high cost.

00:00:35.659 --> 00:00:39.590
Holland's Spider-Man asks Doctor Strange,
played by Benedict Cumberbatch, to make the

00:00:39.590 --> 00:00:41.050
universe forget about him.

00:00:41.050 --> 00:00:44.050
That means everyone he's ever known will forget
about his existence.

00:00:44.050 --> 00:00:48.340
So, before Strange performs the spell, Peter
Parker goes to say goodbye to those who helped

00:00:48.340 --> 00:00:50.589
him, starting with the other Spider-Men.

00:00:50.589 --> 00:00:54.200
It's a heart-wrenching moment because it's
at this point we know it's quite possibly

00:00:54.200 --> 00:00:57.909
the last time we'll see the three live-action
Spider-Men share the screen.

00:00:57.909 --> 00:01:01.219
There's always the chance they could return
in a future installment, but that's far from

00:01:01.219 --> 00:01:02.789
a sure thing at this point.

00:01:02.789 --> 00:01:04.790
For now, it's just goodbye.

00:01:04.790 --> 00:01:08.120
After months of speculation that all three
of them would share the screen together, it

00:01:08.120 --> 00:01:11.710
actually happened, and just as quickly as
it was confirmed, it went away.

00:01:11.710 --> 00:01:12.710
Losing Friends

00:01:12.710 --> 00:01:15.870
Saying goodbye to the other Spider-Men is
tough for audiences to watch, but what comes

00:01:15.870 --> 00:01:18.230
next is far more devastating.

00:01:18.230 --> 00:01:22.330
After all, the MCU's Peter Parker has only
known these other heroes for a few hours.

00:01:22.330 --> 00:01:26.950
Meanwhile, he's been friends with Ned for
years, and dated MJ for a brief, but still

00:01:26.950 --> 00:01:28.540
meaningful, period of time.

00:01:28.540 --> 00:01:32.730
But, as a result of Doctor Strange's spell,
his two best friends will ultimately forget

00:01:32.730 --> 00:01:33.730
about him.

00:01:33.730 --> 00:01:37.470
It's far more emotional than what Peter originally
wanted to happen when he asked Strange for

00:01:37.470 --> 00:01:38.470
help.

00:01:38.470 --> 00:01:41.090
At the beginning of the film, Peter merely
asks the sorcerer to make everyone forget

00:01:41.090 --> 00:01:42.550
that he's Spider-Man.

00:01:42.550 --> 00:01:46.030
He still could've been with MJ, but she wouldn't
have known about his secret identity.

00:01:46.030 --> 00:01:50.160
With this new spell, which is necessary to
prevent forces from other dimensions from

00:01:50.160 --> 00:01:53.710
entering their world, she has to forget about
Peter entirely.

00:01:53.710 --> 00:01:58.070
Peter hugs Ned goodbye and kisses MJ, knowing
this is the last time they'll know about one

00:01:58.070 --> 00:01:59.070
another.

00:01:59.070 --> 00:02:02.770
He has to say goodbye to the best thing that
happened to him in recent memory, and he struggles

00:02:02.770 --> 00:02:03.850
to part with her.

00:02:03.850 --> 00:02:08.320
Near the end of "Spider-Man: No Way Home,"
MJ insists that Peter find her after Doctor

00:02:08.320 --> 00:02:09.830
Strange performs his spell.

00:02:09.830 --> 00:02:13.380
Peter then goes to the coffee shop where she
works, complete with a prepared speech about

00:02:13.380 --> 00:02:14.750
his feelings for her.

00:02:14.750 --> 00:02:18.740
Admittedly, it's a strange way to go about
telling someone something monumental.

00:02:18.740 --> 00:02:22.890
Peter's plan basically hinges on telling MJ,
who doesn't recognize him at this point, that

00:02:22.890 --> 00:02:24.030
he loves her.

00:02:24.030 --> 00:02:27.330
We're betting that no amount of reminiscing
would allow her to recall who Peter Parker

00:02:27.330 --> 00:02:28.500
is, either.

00:02:28.500 --> 00:02:32.450
However, it's how this scene unfolds that's
genuinely gut-wrenching to witness.

00:02:32.450 --> 00:02:36.910
Peter is prepared to tell MJ who he is, but
he notices a wound on her forehead.

00:02:36.910 --> 00:02:40.730
He doesn't say it, but we, as the audience,
can tell what he is thinking.

00:02:40.730 --> 00:02:44.770
He knows that if he tells MJ he's Spider-Man
and continues dating her, he'll only put her

00:02:44.770 --> 00:02:46.250
in more danger.

00:02:46.250 --> 00:02:50.090
After all, she almost died when she fell off
the side of the new Statue of Liberty.

00:02:50.090 --> 00:02:54.520
Peter recognizes the best thing for MJ is
not to know who he is, so he takes his coffee

00:02:54.520 --> 00:02:56.020
and walks away.

00:02:56.020 --> 00:02:59.520
It's a scene that embodies everything about
the mythos of Spider-Man.

00:02:59.520 --> 00:03:03.460
He frequently has to cast aside what he wants
for himself and do what is good for the rest

00:03:03.460 --> 00:03:04.910
of the world.

00:03:04.910 --> 00:03:08.590
There's a significant moment more than halfway
through "Spider-Man: No Way Home."

00:03:08.590 --> 00:03:12.950
Tom Holland's Peter loses someone close to
him, and as a result, he's hesitant to carry

00:03:12.950 --> 00:03:16.660
on his mission of curing the villains before
sending them back to their realities.

00:03:16.660 --> 00:03:20.591
He talks about a person he loved who lost
their life as a result of his actions, and

00:03:20.591 --> 00:03:23.569
both Maguire and Garfield are there to tell
him that he's not alone.

00:03:23.569 --> 00:03:25.319
"I can't save everyone."

00:03:25.319 --> 00:03:28.690
Holland's character tries to tell them they
don't know what he's going through, but little

00:03:28.690 --> 00:03:31.620
does he know, they have experienced all of
the same things.

00:03:31.620 --> 00:03:35.959
Garfield's Spider-Man tells the story of how
he failed to catch Gwen Stacy during a climactic

00:03:35.959 --> 00:03:38.920
battle, as seen at the end of "The Amazing
Spider-Man 2."

00:03:38.920 --> 00:03:42.830
He then describes how his failure caused him
to act more violently, to the point that he

00:03:42.830 --> 00:03:44.599
barely recognized himself.

00:03:44.599 --> 00:03:48.140
Macguire's Peter Parker then shares the story
of his Uncle Ben's murder.

00:03:48.140 --> 00:03:52.560
He recalls how he went down a path of revenge,
tracking down the man responsible and killing

00:03:52.560 --> 00:03:53.560
him.

00:03:53.560 --> 00:03:57.010
To be Peter Parker is to have gone through
unimaginable pain.

00:03:57.010 --> 00:04:00.500
These heartbreaking stories give Holland's
Spider-Man the courage necessary to continue

00:04:00.500 --> 00:04:04.020
with his plan to save the villains rather
than outright killing them.

00:04:04.020 --> 00:04:08.800
The MCU "Spider-Man" films made the decision
not to show the death of Uncle Ben on-screen.

00:04:08.800 --> 00:04:13.080
It's alluded to at various points, leaving
fans to believe that, in doing so, the franchise

00:04:13.080 --> 00:04:17.440
would simply skip over Ben's whole, "With
great power comes great responsibility" speech

00:04:17.440 --> 00:04:19.199
right before his dramatic death.

00:04:19.199 --> 00:04:23.190
This isn't necessarily the case, thanks to
one pivotal Aunt May scene.

00:04:23.190 --> 00:04:27.410
When the villains decide to ambush Tom Holland's
Spider-Man, they really put him through the

00:04:27.410 --> 00:04:28.410
wringer.

00:04:28.410 --> 00:04:30.600
The fight concludes with the Green Goblin
throwing one of his signature Pumpkin Bombs

00:04:30.600 --> 00:04:32.350
at Peter and Aunt May.

00:04:32.350 --> 00:04:33.990
Peter goes to make sure his aunt is all right.

00:04:33.990 --> 00:04:38.010
When he tells her he wants to abandon the
plan, Aunt May reminds him that, With great

00:04:38.010 --> 00:04:41.100
power, there must also come great responsibility.

00:04:41.100 --> 00:04:44.900
It's heartbreaking because the audience can
guess what's going to happen next.

00:04:44.900 --> 00:04:48.530
Aunt May's injuries are too severe, and she
dies in Peter's arms.

00:04:48.530 --> 00:04:52.530
He can't stay there to properly grieve because
the police are on his tail, believing he's

00:04:52.530 --> 00:04:54.730
the one responsible for all of the damage.

00:04:54.730 --> 00:04:59.040
He runs into the night with his biggest supporter
no longer there.

